{"qid":"Q810","names":["Kingdom of Jordan"],"title":"Kingdom of Jordan","endonym":{"native":"االْمَمْلَكَةُ الْأُرْدُنِيَةُ الْهَاشِمِيَة","lang":"ar"},"capsule":"The Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan (المملكة الأردنية الهاشمية) emerged as a fully independent state on 25 May 1946 when the British Mandate of Transjordan ended, though its attested polity boundary begins in 1947 with the formalization of Hashemite rule. Founded by King Abdullah I, who was assassinated in Jerusalem in 1951, Jordan absorbed the West Bank during the 1948 Arab-Israeli War, holding it until Israel's capture in 1967. King Hussein ibn Talal (r. 1952–1999) navigated the Cold War, the 1967 and 1973 Arab-Israeli wars, and expelled the PLO in the 1970 Black September crisis; he signed a formal peace treaty with Israel in 1994. King Abdullah II has ruled since 1999.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Jordan's boundaries are well-attested in international treaties; the West Bank's status as part of Jordan from 1948–1967 and its subsequent exclusion from sovereignty are clearly documented.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Jordan","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Abdullah I of Jordan","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abdullah_I_of_Jordan"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Hussein of Jordan","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hussein_of_Jordan"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Israel–Jordan peace treaty","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel%E2%80%93Jordan_peace_treaty"}],"britannica":"place/Jordan","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Jordan","rulers":[{"qid":"Q192780","name":"Abdullah I of Jordan","start":1946,"end":